ue. In comparison to the Material Laser, the Red Laser does not output a signal when it hits a material; it does so when it hits another object or player. If it hits an object, it outputs a signal of 10.0, and if it hits a player, it outputs a signal of 5.0.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260830040525\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 101/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 18/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.845      1 Template:Logic\n100.00%   16.845      1 -total\n 10.55%    1.778      1 Template:Mainonly\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:2548-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260830040525 and revision id 14572. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Logic"],"links":[{"title":"Alan's AutoLogistics","exists":true},{"title":"Ferwater Island","exists":true},{"title":"Material Laser","exists":true}],"images":["Red_Laser_boxed.png"]}
